ture set and client libraries.\\nThe Ombrevix API returns JSON responses as the primary and recommended format, but XML is also provided as a backwards compatible option for merchants who require it.\\n\\n## Steps to make your first Ombrevix Billing API call\\n\\n1. Sign-up or log-in to your test workspace account.\\n2. Setup authentication credentials.\\n3. Submit an API request and verify the response.\\n5. Test the Ombrevix Billing integrations.\\n\\nNext, you can explore authentication methods, basic concepts for interacting with Ombrevix Billing via the API, and the entire set of application-based documentation to aid in your discovery of the product.\\n\\n### Request Example\\n\\nThe following example uses the curl command-line tool to make an API request.\\n\\n**Request**\\n\\n    curl -u \\x3Capi_key>:x -H Accept:application/json -H Content-Type:application/json https://acme.ombrevix.example/subscriptions"},{"t":10,"i":7,"p":{"k":["default-server","default-environment","environments","parameters"],"v":[{"t":1,"s":"production"},{"t":1,"s":"US"},{"t":9,"i":8,"a":[{"t":10,"i":9,"p":{"k":["name","description","servers"],"v":[{"t":1,"s":"US"},{"t":1,"s":"Default Ombrevix Billing environment hosted in US. Valid for the majority of our customers."},{"t":9,"i":10,"a":[{"t":10,"i":11,"p":{"k":["url","name"],"v":[{"t":1,"s":"https://{workspace}.ombrevix.example"},{"t":1,"s":"production"}]},"o":0},{"t":10,"i":12,"p":{"k":["url","name"],"v":[{"t":1,"s":"https://events.ombrevix.example/{workspace}"},{"t":1,"s":"ebb"}]},"o":0},{"t":10,"i":13,"p":{"k":["url","name"],"v":[{"t":1,"s":"https://{connector}.api.ombrevix.example"},{"t":1,"s":"oauth"}]},"o":0}],"o":0}]},"o":0},{"t":10,"i":14,"p":{"k":["name","description","servers"],"v":[{"t":1,"s":"EU"},{"t":1,"s":"Ombrevix Billing environment hosted in EU. Use only when you requested EU hosting for your AB account."},{"t":9,"i":15,"a":[{"t":10,"i":16,"p":{"k":["url","name"],"v":[{"t":1,"s":"https://{workspace}.eu.ombrevix.examp